<title>UK: Avocet buys Malaysian gold explorer Damar.</title>
<headline>Avocet buys Malaysian gold explorer Damar.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Avocet Mining Plc, the international mining group and largest tungsten producer in the western world, said on Thursday it had bought a 60 percent stake in Malaysian gold exploration company Damar Consolidated Exploration Sdn Bhd.</p>
<p>Avocet said it had an option to buy a further 36.8 percent at any time during the next two years. It said it would pay Damar 1.1 million ordinary shares in Avocet, amounting to around 2.3 million stg at current prices. The additional stake option, if exercised, would cost a further 800,000 ordinary shares.</p>
</text>
